
@c %start of fragment

@node API
@chapter API
The following is the list of modules provided by this library.



@section Module (documenta writer)

@anchor{documenta writer save}@defun save text path
@verbatim
Write TEXT to the file in PATH.

  TEXT (string)
    Arbitrary text.

  PATH (string)
    Absolute or relative path to the file the text will be written to.

  RESULT
    If the file doesn't exist, it will be created and the text will be
    saved to it. If the file exists, its contents will be overwritten.
@end verbatim

@end defun


@section Module (documenta templates)

@anchor{documenta templates stexi:api-chapter}@defun stexi:api-chapter sections
@verbatim
Return a library API as an stexi chapter.

  SECTIONS (list of stexi)
    A list where every item is an stexi section.

  RETURN VALUE (stexi)
    A chapter documenting a library's API.
@end verbatim

@end defun

@anchor{documenta templates stexi:module-section}@defun stexi:module-section module-name
@verbatim
Return the module documentation as an stexi section.

  MODULE-NAME (list of symbols)
    For example: '(mylib amodule).

  RETURN VALUE (stexi)
    A section documenting a module's API.
@end verbatim

@end defun

@anchor{documenta templates text:module-page}@defun text:module-page module-name
Render the API of the given module in plain text.

@end defun



@section Module (documenta data)

@anchor{documenta data file-path->module-name}@defun file-path->module-name file-path lib-parent-path
Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.

@end defun

@anchor{documenta data get-file-paths}@defun get-file-paths directory
@verbatim
Return a list of paths to Scheme files in the given directory.

  Scheme files are identified by their «.scm» extension.

  DIRECTORY (string)
    Absolute path to a directory containing a Guile Scheme library.

  RETURN VALUE (list of string)
    A list where every element represents a path to a Scheme file.
@end verbatim

@end defun



@section Module (documenta cli)

@anchor{documenta cli call}@defun call command spec
@end defun

@anchor{documenta cli spec}@defvar spec
@end defvar



@section Module (documenta commands)

@anchor{documenta commands DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}@defvar DEFAULT_DOC_PATH
@end defvar

@anchor{documenta commands build}@defun build directory [destination]
@verbatim
Build the API documentation for the library in the given directory.

  DIRECTORY (string)
    Absolute or relative path to a directory containing a Guile Scheme
    library.

  DESTINATION (string)
    Optional path to a directory where the documentation should be
    saved. If not provided, the documentation will be saved in the
    current working directory, in a subdirectory called «doc/api».

  RESULT
    A summary report is displayed in the standard output with the
    results of running the test suite. A full report is saved to a log
    file in LOG_PATH.
@end verbatim

@end defun

@c %end of fragment
